## 8. Camada preditiva — 9 scores

Todos os scores retornam:
```js
{
  score: 0-100,
  name: string,         // "Churn Risk"
  code: string,         // "churn_risk_score"
  desc: string,         // descrição curta
  inputs: string[],     // sinais consumidos
  action: string,       // ação recomendada code
  // campos específicos opcionais
}
```

### 8.1 Inventário completo

| # | Nome | Code | Lógica resumida |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Churn Risk | `churn_risk_score` | Penaliza por adherence<60% (-35), checkin_drop>40% (-25), missed sessions; inverte para risk + baseline 15 |
| 2 | Fatigue Risk | `fatigue_risk_score` | 20 base + (Δrpe × 15) max 50 + sleep penalty (18 se <6h, 10 se <7h) |
| 3 | Pain Recurrence | `pain_recurrence_score` | Conta ocorrências de dor lombar × 22 + 10 baseline, cap 100 |
| 4 | Progression Readiness | `progression_readiness_score` | 15 base + adh ok (35/15) + rpe ok (25/5) + pain ok (25/5) |
| 5 | Session Completion | `session_completion_score` | (completed + partial×0.5) / planned × 90 − partial_rate × 30 |
| 6 | Plan Fit | `plan_fit_score` | 85 − partial_rate × 80; flag `fit_issue` se partial > 30% |
| 7 | Recovery Instability | `recovery_instability_score` | sleep penalty (35/20/5) + rpe_high (20/5) + pain_light_recurrent (15/0) |
| 8 | Response Compatibility | `response_compatibility_score` | 60 base + load_delta × 60 + vol_delta × 40 |
| 9 | Plateau Risk | `plateau_risk_score` | load_change_3w: <3%→60, <6%→35, else 15 |

### 8.2 Bandas
```js
function band(score) {
  if (score >= 75) return 'low';
  if (score >= 50) return 'moderate';
  if (score >= 30) return 'high';
  return 'critical';
}
```

> **"Good scores"** (Progression Readiness, Session Completion, Plan Fit, Response Compatibility): invertem semântica — labels passam a ser `BOM/ATENÇÃO/BAIXO`.

### 8.3 Insights gerados (RF-5.10)
4 insights estáticos a partir dos scores. Estrutura:
```js
{
  id, severity: 'positive'|'warning'|'critical'|'info',
  title, data, interpretation, action, score, tag
}
```

Mapeamento severity → cor:
- positive → green
- warning → amber
- critical → coral
- info → cyan

