### 13.2 Globais expostos (Babel scope workaround)
Cada arquivo termina com `Object.assign(window, { ... })` listando explicitamente o que outros arquivos consomem. **Sem isso, scripts type=text/babel não compartilham escopo.**

```js
// perf-atoms.jsx
Object.assign(window, { B, FF_DISPLAY, FF_MONO, Icon, Chip, ChoiceCard, Field, PrivacyNote, Hint, VoiceBar, StepHeader, Slider, ToggleRow });

// perf-engines.jsx
Object.assign(window, { MARIANA, STUDIO_AGG, band, bandColor, readinessBand, computeAllScores, generateInsights });

// perf-screens.jsx
Object.assign(window, { TelaOverview, TelaAderencia, TelaPerformance, TelaDor, TelaScores, TelaVoz, TelaMarcos, Sparkline, BarChart, DualLine, ScoreRing, ScreenWrap, ScreenTitle, Section, StatCard, AIMessage, BodyDiagram });
```

> **Regra crítica:** nunca declarar `const styles = { ... }` no escopo global — usar inline styles ou objetos com nome específico (`perfStyles`, etc.).

